    },
    "forearm": {
      "refs": [
        "forearm",
        "full"
      ],
      "prompt": "Dark storm-grey brushed steel (#3A4250) covered in glowing electric-blue lightning (#3DB8FF) with white-hot cores: jagged branching bolts crackle across the whole forearm, mostly running left to right. Over the steel sit raised polished silver armour shards (#C8CED8): long sharp angular slashes and chevrons slanting diagonally from lower left to upper right, three or four across the forearm, some broken into pieces, with the lightning running round and between them. The two thin strips at the far left are the joint collar: paint them plain flat silver (#C8CCD0)."
    },
